Another NAO ascension!  Read yall's replies (from my earlier Reopening
some Debates post) and decided to go for it.  This is my third
ascension and it was by far the least likely.  Some high points:

Never found a single ring of levitation.  Tinned two tengus, my pet
killed a third and I thought I'd go for the TC.  Ate him.  Felt jumpy.
Ate the other two and nothing.  By that point I was down near Medusa,
wearing dwarven mithril and a CoMR.  I had a bunch of uncursed rings,
so I started trying them on and marking them off as !tc after I jumped
again.  Found another ring!  I was desperate to stop jumping so I just
put it on.  About ten turns later I polymorphed into a kobold, broke my
armor and my cloak, and discovered it was a cursed =oPoly.  So I
started trying on those !tc rings and luckily one was Poly Control.
Found some more elven mithril, polyed myself into a Titan (cause they
fly!), and took out Medusa.  I'd switched genders at some point, so I
made a bunch of pets - grey and silver baby dragons.  Named them
(cleverly!) Grey1, Grey2, etc.

Myself the Titan and the grey and silver horde then took out the
castle.  Got the desperately-needed WoW and some lev boots, then headed
back up to the only altar, in Minetown to get kitted up.  Wand was 0:1,
so GDSM, speed boots, Greyswandir, and a =oConflict.  Then I laid a few
stoning grenades and tucked them away.  My horde (now greatly reduced
in size) ate the coaligned priest so I got +oEH and a robe.

Somewhere in there I found a =TC, but I didn't really need it - the
next time I went downstairs, a gremlin had spawned in Medusa's level.
And you know what that means - 50 gremlins by the time I could get over
to it.  One of them hit me, chucked, and I felt less jumpy.  I chucked
too, actually, since that was the only intrinsic they got.

Cleared Ludios, got the ludicrous gold from it and from my dead
minetown priest, and bought protection from VotD priest up to naked
-11!  How exciting!

Cleared Gehennom.  I decided pretty early on that I couldn't deal with
L so I b?G'd them and didn't feel the least bit guilty.  I got a throne
geno too and picked disenchanters - they are my favorite single-species
genocide.

Back up to the altar to sacrifice some.  I'm not sure why - I wanted to
get crowned for some reason.  I changed my mind on that eventually...
used up two wands and ended up with a bunch of peacefuls.  So I let my
pet grey D and guardian naga out of the room they were locked up in -
didn't want them to get hungry.  I stole a couple of kills from the
greedy guts, but the last one was a dwarf king.
I was a dwarf.
Woops.  There goes the 11 points of protection.  And no more priests.
Double woops.
Next thing I found to kill was a grey unicorn so at least I converted
the altar back and mollified Quetzal (the God of Sucky Artifacts).
Moving on!

The wiz sucked a lot.  The mysterious force sucked a lot.  I did
remember to c?Tele out of Rodney's tower and then c!oGL out of the
Sanctum, so I suppose I am improving a bit.  ;)  The Planes sucked
really bad too.  Got down to 47 hp on Air, fainting, surrounded by E
and Rodney, so I prayed, got my tummy happy, whacked @ with a stoning
grenade, quaffed a potion, put on the ring of rengeration and hid in an
energy vortex.  There was a MMF there too and I forgot all my rings.
Sigh.  I knew the blessed one was conflict, and I remembered the inv
letter of poly control, so I just trial-and-errored FA and regen.
Water was even worse because I read a CURSED ?oGD and couldn't find the
portal.  Hundreds of turns there.  Argh.

I tried to be good on Astral but Pest almost got me so I caused
conflict.  First altar was Neutral, second was Lawful which is good
because I was ready to use that HoOA at that point.  I went to my
reward wielding two beers, which that poor dwarf surely deserved.  I
used 7 !oFH, for the record.  :(



